From cf35437fbcc39dac3786ec48515cc8d62bc81b8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:50:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/47] Z 6III: the sensor streams -- live view starts and runs
 frame by frame

CaptureSequence powers the sensor and gives the front end 1 s to report
ready (CSEQEV10 bit 3, else error 0x1EA7). Four things stood between them:

- The battery data line. The MCU's fuel-gauge task polls PD13 and only
  talks to the battery after reading it high; the floating 0 made it give
  up after 300 polls (~2.8 s), and only then did the power report (family
  4 kind 3) reach the EXPEED, whose start sequence waits for it before it
  asks for live view. mcu-pins now defaults to D13=1, the line's idle
  level; FrontEnd's mode-1 start moves from ~4 s to ~1.3 s.
- Engine 0x150c's start acknowledgement. The job thread waits, for jobs
  that enable engine bit 1, for +0x24c bits 5 and 6 on INTID 0x107 before
  it tells FrontEnd 0x41D0001, which FrontEnd's 400 ms wait needs.
  ../z9-qemu models that bank for its Zr profile (zr-primary-bank1-model);
  the attachment section wires it on this board and raises the two bits
  when engine bit 1 becomes active. They cannot be frame events: the
  sensor is only started after the ready report this unblocks.
- The sensor's control port: SIO instance 8 (logical channel 6), register
  writes as 0x81/address/data, each transfer waited on. Attached as a
  write-only sink (default sio-sink=9:8); its read command 0x82 is used
  only by adjustment handlers not reached.
- SDES channel words: event1508-aux-config-model (retention of +0/+4/+8/
  +0xc) and event1508-aux-status-input of zeros (error status reads "no
  error") join the defaults.

With these, CSEQ starts the SDES channel (sub_40C29DF8 -> IF +0x10), the
z9 frame-timing model streams, the sensor-IF interrupt fires every ~35 ms,
the sensor module and CSEQ log every frame, and engine 0x150c takes a
statistics job whose first frame the statistics model fills.

The error dialog that remains on the original body is not this path: the
first sensor power-up checks the version bytes of the sensor parameter
record (record 0x63, +0x117ab4), which the RAM-derived SNOR_USER body
holds as zeros (as it holds most of that record), and reports error 0x45.
z63-tools/snor_user_sensor_version.py writes a copy with a declared
version (0x160). gdb_probe/mcu_probe LIGHT lines carry host seconds;
mcu_probe gains MEMR=r:n.

Still to do: the display shows nothing over live view yet (the GUI draws
no shooting screen once live view runs; the image pipeline has no output).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
